      "answer": "$y=\\frac38x+\\frac52$",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Rewrite as $(3x+4)^{1/2}$. — B1 or equivalent.\n$\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac12(3x+4)^{-1/2}\\times3$. — B1. Guidance: must have multiplication by 3.\nAt $x=4$, $\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac38$, seen or implied. — B1.\nForm a line through $(4,4)$ with gradient $3/8$. — M1. Guidance: if $y\\neq4$ is used, clear evidence of substituting $x=4$ is needed.\n$y-4=\\frac38(x-4)$, or $y=\\frac38x+\\frac52$. — A1.\nTotal: 5",
