      "answer": "$\\frac59$",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Area under the line $=\\frac12(4)(4+5/2)=13$, or $\\int_0^4(3x/8+5/2)\\,dx=13$. — B1.\nFor the curve, $\\int(3x+4)^{1/2}\\,dx=\\frac{(3x+4)^{3/2}}{3/2}[\\div3]$. — B1B1. Guidance: allow as part of the difference of two integrals; first B1 for the integral without division by 3, second B1 requires division by 3.\nApply limits $0$ to $4$ to obtain $128/9-16/9=112/9=12\\frac49$. — M1.\nArea $=13-12\\frac49=\\frac59$, or $0.556$. — A1.\nAlternative using horizontal strips: triangular area between tangent and axes $=\\frac12\\times4\\times\\frac32=3$, or equivalent integral. — B1.\nArea between curve and axes using $x=(y^2-4)/3$: integrate from $y=2$ to $4$. — B1B1.\nApply limits to obtain $32/9$. — M1.\nArea $=32/9-3=5/9$, or $0.556$. — A1.\nTotal: 5",
